  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 414 PM EDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nAmplifying ridging out west will bring northwesterly flow over the \nOhio Valley. Multiple systems riding along the ridge will cause \ndaily chances for showers and storms Wednesday through Friday. \nPlenty of moisture and warm temperatures in the upper 80s will allow \nfor ample instability each day. Shear will be weak to sufficient, \nindicating a chance for some strong to severe storms each day. \n\nGoing into the weekend, a front will stall in the Ohio Valley \nvicinity as ridging build over the southeastern CONUS. Depending on \nwhere the front stalls will determine the precip chances through the \nweekend. South and along the front, we will see scattered showers \nand storms (some strong to severe possible).",
